  <diagram id="p9" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel grid="0" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1920" pageHeight="1080" background="#ffffff" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p9_3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8f9fa;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&#39;text-align:left;padding:8px;&#39;&gt;&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:14px;color:#1a365d;&#39;&gt;1. Questions (with SRS Section References)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;     &lt;ol style=&#39;line-height:1.5;margin-top:4px;&#39;&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.1 — Branch Managers]:&lt;/b&gt; Does Head Office only need the current branch manager&#39;s start date, or a complete historical log of all previous managers who ran each branch?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.2 — Training]:&lt;/b&gt; What is the minimum passing score out of 100 for training courses (fixed e.g. 60%, or configured per course)?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.3, 7.8 &amp; 7.9 — Custom Luxury Pricing]:&lt;/b&gt; When a luxury vehicle has its own custom daily rate (COO Note), do corporate category discounts or promo codes still apply to that rate?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.5 — GPS Tracking]:&lt;/b&gt; If a GPS tracker is replaced, should we keep a history of past device installations per vehicle or only the currently installed tracker?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.7 &amp; Section 8 — Corporate Drivers as Individual Customers]:&lt;/b&gt; Should an Authorized Driver who also rents personally have a linked profile to their Individual Customer record, or stay independent?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.10 — Loyalty Program]:&lt;/b&gt; What is the exact formula for earning points on a completed rental and the EGP discount conversion rate when redeeming points?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.12 — Rentals]:&lt;/b&gt; How is the late return fee calculated (hourly vs. daily multiplier), and can a corporate rental also add external non-employee Additional Drivers?&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.16 — Monthly Corporate Billing]:&lt;/b&gt; When Finance sends a single monthly invoice to corporate clients, does a single payment settle multiple rentals via a consolidated Invoice entity?&lt;/li&gt;     &lt;/ol&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="235" width="1600" x="40" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_4" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffdf5;strokeColor=#d6b656;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&#39;text-align:left;padding:8px;&#39;&gt;&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:14px;color:#1a365d;&#39;&gt;2. Assumptions (with SRS Section References)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;     &lt;ol style=&#39;line-height:1.45;margin-top:4px;&#39;&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.1 — Branches &amp; Hours]:&lt;/b&gt; Each branch stores its current manager (&lt;code&gt;ManagerEmpID&lt;/code&gt;) and &lt;code&gt;ManagerStartDate&lt;/code&gt;. Airport branches working 24/7 use &lt;code&gt;Is24Hours = 1&lt;/code&gt; with nullable &lt;code&gt;OpeningHour&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;ClosingHour&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.1 — Employee Specialization]:&lt;/b&gt; Because an employee cannot be both an agent and a mechanic and other staff (accountants, drivers, cleaners) exist, specialization into &lt;code&gt;RENTAL_AGENT&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;MECHANIC&lt;/code&gt; is modeled as &lt;b&gt;Disjoint and Partial&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.2 — Training Attempts]:&lt;/b&gt; Since failed courses can be retaken and HR keeps every attempt, &lt;code&gt;TRAINING_ATTEMPT&lt;/code&gt; uses composite PK &lt;code&gt;(EmpID, CourseCode, AttemptNo)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.3 — Models &amp; Luxury Pricing]:&lt;/b&gt; Surrogate key &lt;code&gt;ModelID&lt;/code&gt; identifies &lt;code&gt;CAR_MODEL&lt;/code&gt;. Nullable &lt;code&gt;CustomDailyRate&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE&lt;/code&gt; supports luxury cars with custom prices (COO Note); if NULL, the active category rate applies.&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.3 &amp; 7.6 — Vehicle Location &amp; Audit]:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE&lt;/code&gt; stores both &lt;code&gt;HomeBranchCode&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;CurrentBranchCode&lt;/code&gt; (Objective O-1), and &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE_STATUS_LOG&lt;/code&gt; records every status change with employee and timestamp (Objective O-3).&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.7 — Customers]:&lt;/b&gt; Customer specialization into &lt;code&gt;INDIVIDUAL_CUSTOMER&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;CORPORATE_CUSTOMER&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;b&gt;Disjoint and Total&lt;/b&gt;. Corporate drivers renting personally have an independent &lt;code&gt;INDIVIDUAL_CUSTOMER&lt;/code&gt; account.&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.10 — Loyalty Points &amp; Tier]:&lt;/b&gt; Total points and Tier (&lt;code&gt;Silver &amp;lt;1000&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Gold 1000–4999&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Platinum &amp;gt;=5000&lt;/code&gt;) are modeled as derived attributes computed from &lt;code&gt;LOYALTY_TRANSACTION&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.12, 7.15 &amp; 7.16 — Rentals, Suppliers &amp; Payments]:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;code&gt;AppliedDailyRate&lt;/code&gt; is snapshotted on &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt;; surrogate keys &lt;code&gt;SupplierID&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;LoyaltyTxID&lt;/code&gt; are used where natural keys were not specified.&lt;/li&gt;     &lt;/ol&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="1600" x="40" y="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_5" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff5f5;strokeColor=#b85450;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&#39;text-align:left;padding:8px;&#39;&gt;&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:14px;color:#1a365d;&#39;&gt;3. Contradictions (Both Sections &amp; What They Say)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;     &lt;ol style=&#39;line-height:1.5;margin-top:4px;&#39;&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.3 Main Text vs. Section 7.3 COO Note — Category vs. Vehicle Pricing]:&lt;/b&gt; Section 7.3 states &lt;i&gt;&quot;Pricing is set per category as a daily rate... Customers book a category&quot;&lt;/i&gt;, whereas the COO Note states &lt;i&gt;&quot;Some of our luxury cars, like the Mercedes S-Class, don&#39;t follow the category price. They have their own price.&quot;&lt;/i&gt; (Resolved by adding optional &lt;code&gt;CustomDailyRate&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.7 vs. Section 8 Ms. Rana Adel Interview — Authorized Drivers]:&lt;/b&gt; Section 7.7 states corporate authorized drivers &lt;i&gt;&quot;are only known through their company&quot;&lt;/i&gt;, whereas Section 8 states &lt;i&gt;&quot;Some corporate drivers are also individual customers with us... rents for his family on his own account.&quot;&lt;/i&gt; (Resolved by keeping Corporate Authorized Driver records scoped to the company while allowing personal Individual Customer accounts).&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.16 Main Text vs. Section 7.16 Finance Note — Per-Rental Payment vs. Monthly Corporate Invoice]:&lt;/b&gt; Section 7.16 models payments per rental (deposit at pickup, final payment at return), whereas the Finance Note states &lt;i&gt;&quot;Our corporate clients usually don&#39;t pay per rental. We send them one invoice at the end of every month.&quot;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;       &lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Section 7.1 Sentence 3 vs. Sentence 4 &amp; NFR-2 — Fixed Opening Hours vs. 24/7 Airport Branches]:&lt;/b&gt; Section 7.1 states &lt;i&gt;&quot;Branches have fixed daily opening and closing hours&quot;&lt;/i&gt;, then immediately states airport branches work around the clock (24/7). (Resolved via &lt;code&gt;Is24Hours&lt;/code&gt; flag and nullable hours).&lt;/li&gt;     &lt;/ol&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="215" width="1600" x="40" y="595" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="p10" name="4-Business-Rules">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1635" dy="1016" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1920" pageHeight="1080" background="#ffffff" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p10_3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#1a365d;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;div style=&#39;text-align:left;padding:8px;&#39;&gt;&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:14px;color:#1a365d;&#39;&gt;Part D — Business Rules That Cannot Be Enforced by PK, FK, NOT NULL, UNIQUE, CHECK, or DEFAULT Alone&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;     &lt;table border=&#39;1&#39; cellspacing=&#39;0&#39; cellpadding=&#39;8&#39; style=&#39;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:11px;border-color:#cbd5e0;&#39;&gt;       &lt;thead style=&#39;background-color:#1a365d;color:#ffffff;&#39;&gt;         &lt;tr&gt;           &lt;th width=&#39;4%&#39;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;           &lt;th width=&#39;12%&#39;&gt;SRS Section&lt;/th&gt;           &lt;th width=&#39;24%&#39;&gt;Business Rule&lt;/th&gt;           &lt;th width=&#39;30%&#39;&gt;Why Constraints (PK, FK, NN, UQ, CK, DF) Are Not Enough&lt;/th&gt;           &lt;th width=&#39;30%&#39;&gt;How to Enforce It (Trigger, Stored Procedure, or Application Logic)&lt;/th&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;       &lt;/thead&gt;       &lt;tbody&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#ffffff;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.7 Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A blacklisted customer cannot make a new reservation or sign a new rental agreement.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;RESERVATION&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt; only store &lt;code&gt;CustomerNo&lt;/code&gt;. A SQL &lt;code&gt;CHECK&lt;/code&gt; constraint cannot query another table (&lt;code&gt;CUSTOMER.IsBlacklisted&lt;/code&gt;) to verify the customer&#39;s status.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;BEFORE INSERT Trigger&lt;/b&gt; on &lt;code&gt;RESERVATION&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt; (and check in &lt;code&gt;sp_CreateBooking&lt;/code&gt;) that queries &lt;code&gt;CUSTOMER.IsBlacklisted&lt;/code&gt; and aborts with an error if &lt;code&gt;IsBlacklisted = 1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#f8fafc;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.9 Promotions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A promo code can only be applied if the reservation date is within its validity period and its total uses have not reached &lt;code&gt;MaxUses&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;Requires cross-table date comparison against &lt;code&gt;PROMOTION(ValidFrom, ValidTo)&lt;/code&gt; and an aggregate &lt;code&gt;COUNT(*)&lt;/code&gt; across all existing rows in &lt;code&gt;RESERVATION&lt;/code&gt;, neither of which a row-level &lt;code&gt;CHECK&lt;/code&gt; constraint can perform.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Trigger / Stored Procedure (&lt;code&gt;sp_ApplyPromoCode&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/b&gt; that locks the &lt;code&gt;PROMOTION&lt;/code&gt; row, checks validity dates, counts active reservations using that code, and rejects if &lt;code&gt;COUNT(*) &amp;gt;= MaxUses&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#ffffff;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.1 Staff &amp;amp; 7.7 Blacklist&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;An employee cannot be both a Rental Agent and a Mechanic (disjoint subtypes), and only a Branch Manager can blacklist a customer.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;Separate subtype tables (&lt;code&gt;RENTAL_AGENT&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;MECHANIC&lt;/code&gt;) cannot use standard single-table constraints to check if the same &lt;code&gt;EmpID&lt;/code&gt; already exists in the sibling table, nor verify that &lt;code&gt;BlacklistedByMgrID&lt;/code&gt; is in &lt;code&gt;BRANCH.ManagerEmpID&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;BEFORE INSERT Triggers&lt;/b&gt; on &lt;code&gt;RENTAL_AGENT&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;MECHANIC&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;CUSTOMER&lt;/code&gt; verifying role exclusivity and checking that &lt;code&gt;BlacklistedByMgrID&lt;/code&gt; is an active branch manager.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#f8fafc;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.6 Transfers &amp;amp; Sec. 8&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A vehicle transfer&#39;s &lt;code&gt;FromBranchCode&lt;/code&gt; must match the vehicle&#39;s actual &lt;code&gt;CurrentBranchCode&lt;/code&gt;, and completing a transfer must update &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE.CurrentBranchCode&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;CurrentOdometer&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A &lt;code&gt;CHECK&lt;/code&gt; constraint on &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE_TRANSFER&lt;/code&gt; can enforce &lt;code&gt;FromBranchCode &amp;lt;&amp;gt; ToBranchCode&lt;/code&gt;, but cannot inspect or update &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE.CurrentBranchCode&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE.CurrentOdometer&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Transactional Stored Procedure (&lt;code&gt;sp_TransferVehicle&lt;/code&gt;) + AFTER INSERT Trigger&lt;/b&gt; on &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE_TRANSFER&lt;/code&gt; validating current branch/odometer and updating the &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE&lt;/code&gt; row atomically.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#ffffff;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.7 &amp;amp; 7.8 Corporate Credit Limit&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A corporate customer cannot open new rentals if their outstanding unpaid balance exceeds their approved &lt;code&gt;CreditLimit&lt;/code&gt;, and category discounts apply only within contract dates.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;Computing outstanding balance requires summing charges across multiple &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt; rows minus &lt;code&gt;PAYMENT&lt;/code&gt; rows across tables, which declarative constraints cannot compute.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored Procedure (&lt;code&gt;sp_CreateCorporateRental&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/b&gt; that calculates total unpaid exposure against &lt;code&gt;CORPORATE_CUSTOMER.CreditLimit&lt;/code&gt; and fetches active discounts from &lt;code&gt;CORPORATE_CONTRACT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#f8fafc;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.12 Rentals &amp;amp; 7.3 Status Audit&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A rented vehicle must currently have status &lt;code&gt;&#39;Available&#39;&lt;/code&gt; at the pickup branch; any change to &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE.Status&lt;/code&gt; must record the employee and timestamp in &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE_STATUS_LOG&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;Cross-table validation between &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE&lt;/code&gt; and automatic audit row insertion into &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE_STATUS_LOG&lt;/code&gt; cannot be done with declarative constraints.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;AFTER UPDATE Trigger&lt;/b&gt; on &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE(Status)&lt;/code&gt; that automatically inserts an audit record into &lt;code&gt;VEHICLE_STATUS_LOG&lt;/code&gt;, and checkout procedure verifying &lt;code&gt;Status = &#39;Available&#39;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#ffffff;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.14 Traffic Violations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;A traffic violation matched to a rental must have &lt;code&gt;ViolationDT&lt;/code&gt; falling between that rental&#39;s &lt;code&gt;PickupDT&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ActualReturnDT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;ViolationDT&lt;/code&gt; is in &lt;code&gt;TRAFFIC_VIOLATION&lt;/code&gt; while &lt;code&gt;PickupDT&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ActualReturnDT&lt;/code&gt; are in &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt;; a &lt;code&gt;CHECK&lt;/code&gt; constraint cannot span two tables.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE Trigger&lt;/b&gt; on &lt;code&gt;TRAFFIC_VIOLATION&lt;/code&gt; that joins &lt;code&gt;RENTAL&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;RentalNo&lt;/code&gt; and verifies &lt;code&gt;ViolationDT BETWEEN PickupDT AND ActualReturnDT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;         &lt;tr style=&#39;background-color:#f8fafc;&#39;&gt;           &lt;td align=&#39;center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;8&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.10 Loyalty Program&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;An individual customer cannot redeem more loyalty points than their current net balance (&lt;code&gt;SUM(Earned) - SUM(Redeemed)&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;Requires aggregating all historical rows for that customer in &lt;code&gt;LOYALTY_TRANSACTION&lt;/code&gt; before allowing a new &lt;code&gt;Redeemed&lt;/code&gt; row.&lt;/td&gt;           &lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;BEFORE INSERT Trigger&lt;/b&gt; on &lt;code&gt;LOYALTY_TRANSACTION&lt;/code&gt; (for &lt;code&gt;TxType = &#39;Redeemed&#39;&lt;/code&gt;) that calculates net points balance and blocks redemption if &lt;code&gt;Points &amp;gt; NetBalance&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;         &lt;/tr&gt;       &lt;/tbody&gt;     &lt;/table&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="680" width="1600" x="40" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
